# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored — the real key must NEVER
# be committed, pasted into a source file, or echoed into a log or a commit message.
#
# Used ONLY by the art-generation script (`scripts/art/`, built 2026-09-21 by PLAN.md #3; the
# authority is docs/ART-BIBLE.md §1c, not UI-DESIGN §9, which is superseded).
#
#   npm run art -- --help       what it can do
#   npm run art -- --stage 1    a DRY RUN: what it would send and what it would cost
#
# This file is NOT read on a dry run, and not read at all until everything that can fail for free
# already has (an unknown asset id, a missing prompt, a --resume naming a run that does not exist).
# Generating needs BOTH --confirm-spend and an explicit asset selection; --preview and --dry-run
# each force a dry run from anywhere. Once loaded, the key is held in a
# wrapper that prints `[redacted]` under every string conversion, and it reaches the network only
# as the `x-goog-api-key` header — never a URL, never a request body, never a log line.
# The game itself needs no keys at all: the narrator is a local model, downloaded once on
# first run, then fully offline. See docs/SHIPPING.md.
# Nothing in the test suite reads this.

GOOGLE_API_KEY=
